# Set one or both — whichever free key(s) you have. Groq is tried first;
# if it fails for any reason (rate limit, quota, error), it automatically
# falls back to Gemini. Leave both blank to run fully offline (Q&A falls
# back to a keyword-based matcher, no LLM needed).
#
# WITHIN each provider, a lighter fallback model is also tried on the SAME
# key before moving to the next provider — Groq and (especially) Gemini's
# free tier meter request quota PER MODEL, not per account, so a 429 on
# the primary model still leaves a lighter model with its own full quota.
# Override the fallback list per provider with a comma-separated
# *_MODEL_FALLBACKS env (empty string = no fallback model, go straight to
# the next provider); otherwise sane defaults are used.

# Groq — free, instant key, no card (https://console.groq.com/keys)
# pip install groq
# openai/gpt-oss-120b = OpenAI's open-weight GPT model, hosted on Groq
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# GROQ_MODEL_FALLBACKS=llama-3.1-8b-instant

# Gemini — free, instant key via Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey)
# pip install google-generativeai
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACKS=gemini-2.0-flash-lite,gemini-2.0-flash
